# Owner-directed handling of internal blockers

- Continue authorized work without routine confirmation requests.
- If an expected field, inferred requirement, uncertain bank action, or other
  self-imposed constraint blocks progress, pause before another live attempt.
  Explain the observed fact and the internal expectation, then check with the owner.
- Do not repeatedly probe a live provider or revise assumptions in a debugging
  loop without that check. After the owner authorizes a specific fix and verification,
  complete that scope; pause again if a new mismatch or constraint appears.
- Mandatory transaction-specific Telegram approval, required bank-app authorization,
  exact destination checks and uncertain-outcome protections remain compulsory.
